  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance alimentaire au Nord-Kivu et r&#xE9;habilitation des axes routiers et am&#xE9;lioration de l&#x2019;acc&#xE8;s a&#xE9;rien au Sud Kivu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide emergency food security assistance to to newly displaced people, inside and outside displacement camps; it also aims to ensure uninterrupted common services to reach affected people. This WFP project provides unconditional, in kind food assistance, in close coordination with FAO; reinstates access to enclaved areas in Kalehe and Minova by rehabilitating key road sections; and ensure UNHAS services to the Hauts Plateaux in South Kivu. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 19,000 people, including 7,230 women, 4,760 children, and including 570 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
